      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Functionality \u0026 Code Simplicity (`DfuRecoverToIdle` \u0026 `DfuClearIfInError`):**\n\n1. **Recovering from busy download states (`lines 397–422`):** When an earlier transfer was interrupted while a block was still being programmed (`kDfuDnloadSync` or `kDfuDnloadBusy`):\n   - Calling `DfuGetStatus(interface)` at line 398 and then immediately calling `DfuPollIdle(interface)` at line 417 issues a second `DFU_GETSTATUS` without sleeping the first response\u0027s `poll_timeout` (which violates the USB DFU `dfuDNBUSY` polling interval).\n   - When that in-flight block finishes, `DfuPollIdle(interface)` settles in `kDfuDnloadIdle` (not `kDfuIdle`), and returning `{}` at line 420 without sending `DFU_ABORT` leaves the device in `dfuDNLOAD-IDLE`.\n2. **Single `DFU_GETSTATUS` in `DfuClearIfInError` (`lines 374–395` \u0026 `517–518`):** Logging `bStatus`/`bState` inside `DfuClearIfInError` before sending `DfuRequest::kClrStatus` avoids calling `DfuGetStatus` twice in a row on line 517–518 and lets you drop `DfuReportStatus`, `DfuClearStatus`, and `DfuAbort`:\n\n```cpp\nvoid RtsUsbDevice::DfuClearIfInError(int interface) {\n  auto status \u003d DfuGetStatus(interface);\n\n  if (status \u0026\u0026 status-\u003estate \u003d\u003d DfuState::kDfuError) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"Device DFU status: bStatus\u003d{:#04x}, bState\u003d{}\",\n                 std::to_underlying(status-\u003estatus),\n                 std::to_underlying(status-\u003estate));\n    DfuSendRequest(DfuRequest::kClrStatus, 0, interface);\n  }\n}\n\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, RtsError\u003e RtsUsbDevice::DfuRecoverToIdle(int interface) {\n  auto status \u003d DfuGetStatus(interface);\n  if (!status) {\n    return std::unexpected(status.error());\n  }\n\n  if (status-\u003estate \u003d\u003d DfuState::kDfuError) {\n    // CLRSTATUS is only valid here.\n    return DfuSendRequest(DfuRequest::kClrStatus, 0, interface);\n  }\n  if (status-\u003estate \u003d\u003d DfuState::kDfuUploadIdle) {\n    return DfuSendRequest(DfuRequest::kAbort, 0, interface);\n  }\n\n  DfuState settled \u003d status-\u003estate;\n  if (settled !\u003d DfuState::kDfuIdle \u0026\u0026 settled !\u003d DfuState::kDfuDnloadIdle) {\n    sleep_(std::min(std::max(status-\u003epoll_timeout, kDfuMinPollDelay),\n                    std::chrono::milliseconds(kUsbDfuTimeout)));\n    auto idle \u003d DfuPollIdle(interface);\n    if (!idle) {\n      return std::unexpected(idle.error());\n    }\n    settled \u003d *idle;\n  }\n  if (settled \u003d\u003d DfuState::kDfuDnloadIdle) {\n    return DfuSendRequest(DfuRequest::kAbort, 0, interface);\n  }\n  return {};\n}\n```\n\nAlso in `DfuDownload()` at **lines 487–492**, please verify that per-block polling settles in `kDfuDnloadIdle`:\n```cpp\n    // Poll status to wait for the block to be processed.\n    if (auto idle \u003d DfuPollIdle(interface);\n        !idle || *idle !\u003d DfuState::kDfuDnloadIdle) {\n      std::println(stderr, \"DFU status error after block {} (offset {:#x}).\",\n                   block_num, offset);\n      DfuClearIfInError(interface);\n      return std::unexpected(idle ? RtsError::kProtocolError : idle.error());\n    }\n```\n\nOther locations in this file:\n- **Lines 487–492** (`DfuDownload` per-block poll check)\n- **Lines 517–518** (`DfuDownload` ZLP error handling—remove `DfuReportStatus(interface);`)\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/b2c5d976-5204-4274-85f0-ebbdd5e79b54)",
