      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Code Simplicity \u0026 Type Safety (`DfuStatusResponse` \u0026 Single-Use Private Wrappers):**\n\n1. **Typed `status` and `state` on `DfuStatusResponse`:** Storing `DfuStatus status` and `DfuState state` directly on `DfuStatusResponse` (converting once in `FromBytes`) eliminates the repeated `static_cast\u003cDfuState\u003e(status-\u003estate)` and `std::to_underlying(DfuStatus::kOk)` / `std::to_underlying(DfuState::kDfuError)` casts across `DfuPollIdle()`, `DfuClearIfInError()`, and `DfuRecoverToIdle()`:\n```cpp\n// The six-byte DFU_GETSTATUS response.\nstruct DfuStatusResponse {\n  DfuStatus status \u003d DfuStatus::kOk;\n  std::chrono::milliseconds poll_timeout{0};\n  DfuState state \u003d DfuState::kDfuIdle;\n\n  // Decodes the response; bwPollTimeout is a 24-bit little-endian value.\n  static DfuStatusResponse FromBytes(\n      std::span\u003cconst uint8_t, kDfuGetStatusResponseLen\u003e raw);\n};\n```\n2. **Remove thin pass-through wrappers (`lines 272–288`):** `DfuClearStatus()` and `DfuAbort()` are single-line wrappers around `DfuSendRequest(DfuRequest::kClrStatus, 0, interface)` and `DfuSendRequest(DfuRequest::kAbort, 0, interface)`, and `DfuReportStatus()` can be folded into `DfuClearIfInError()` so `DfuDownload()` does not issue two back-to-back `DFU_GETSTATUS` requests when the final ZLP stalls.\n3. **Test coverage for `RtsError::kDeviceRejected` (`lines 36, 57–58`):** Please include `RtsError::kDeviceRejected` in `RtsErrorTest.ToStringCoversAllValues` (`rts5817_usb_device_test.cc:388–394`).\n\nOther locations in this file:\n- **Lines 36, 57–58** (`RtsError::kDeviceRejected`)\n- **Lines 272–288** (`DfuClearStatus`, `DfuAbort`, `DfuReportStatus`)\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/b2c5d976-5204-4274-85f0-ebbdd5e79b54)",
