      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Testing, Idiomaticity \u0026 Boundary Coverage:**\n\n1. **Eliminate loop \u0026 weak `EXPECT_LE` oracle in `TimesOutWhenDeviceStaysBusy` (`lines 1090–1103`):** `EXPECT_LE(total, milliseconds(kUsbDfuTimeout))` would pass even if `DfuPollIdle()` never slept (`total \u003d\u003d 0`). Setting `fake_.poll_timeout \u003d milliseconds(25000); fake_.busy_polls \u003d 3;` tests both normal `poll_timeout` sleeps and the `kUsbDfuTimeout - slept` clamping boundary in 3 iterations without a `for` loop:\n```cpp\nTEST_F(RtsUsbDeviceDownloadTest, TimesOutWhenDeviceStaysBusy) {\n  fake_.poll_timeout \u003d milliseconds(25000);\n  fake_.busy_polls \u003d 3;\n\n  auto res \u003d device_-\u003eDfuDownload(std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e{1, 2});\n\n  ASSERT_FALSE(res);\n  EXPECT_EQ(res.error(), RtsError::kTimeout);\n  EXPECT_EQ(slept_, (std::vector\u003cmilliseconds\u003e{\n                        milliseconds(25000),\n                        milliseconds(25000),\n                        milliseconds(10000),\n                    }));\n}\n```\n2. **Assert exact request sequence in `DetachesAfterManifestSoDeviceBoots` (`lines 996–1005`):** Replace `ASSERT_FALSE` + `back()` + `std::count(fake_.requests.begin(), fake_.requests.end(), ...)` with a single exact vector comparison:\n```cpp\nTEST_F(RtsUsbDeviceDownloadTest, DetachesAfterManifestSoDeviceBoots) {\n  ASSERT_TRUE(device_-\u003eDfuDownload(std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e{1, 2}));\n\n  // Download block 0 and the ZLP, and only then DFU_DETACH.\n  EXPECT_EQ(fake_.requests,\n            (std::vector\u003cDfuRequest\u003e{DfuRequest::kDownload,\n                                     DfuRequest::kDownload,\n                                     DfuRequest::kDetach}));\n}\n```\n3. **Specify exact contract arguments instead of `_` matchers** in `ShortWriteIsAnError` (`lines 910–911`), `DetachFailureIsReported` (`lines 1008–1012`), `FailsWhenRecoveryStatusReadFails` (`line 1056`), and `ReportsShortStatusRead` (`line 1067`), and use `fake_.error_on_fail \u003d true;` in `ClearsStatusWhenDeviceIsInErrorState` (`lines 929–945`):\n```cpp\nTEST_F(RtsUsbDeviceDownloadTest, ShortWriteIsAnError) {\n  EXPECT_CALL(*backend_,\n              ControlTransferOut(kBmReqH2dClsIf,\n                                 std::to_underlying(DfuRequest::kDownload), 0,\n                                 kDfuIf, SizeIs(kTransferSize),\n                                 milliseconds(kUsbDfuTimeout)))\n      .WillOnce(Return(std::expected\u003csize_t, int\u003e(kTransferSize - 1)));\n\n  auto res \u003d device_-\u003eDfuDownload(std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6});\n\n  ASSERT_FALSE(res);\n  EXPECT_EQ(res.error(), RtsError::kProtocolError);\n}\n\nTEST_F(RtsUsbDeviceDownloadTest, ClearsStatusWhenDeviceIsInErrorState) {\n  fake_.fail_block \u003d 0;\n  fake_.error_on_fail \u003d true;\n\n  EXPECT_FALSE(device_-\u003eDfuDownload(std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e{1, 2, 3, 4}));\n  EXPECT_EQ(fake_.state_when_cleared,\n            (std::vector\u003cDfuState\u003e{DfuState::kDfuError}));\n}\n\nTEST_F(RtsUsbDeviceDownloadTest, DetachFailureIsReported) {\n  EXPECT_CALL(*backend_,\n              ControlTransferOut(kBmReqH2dClsIf,\n                                 std::to_underlying(DfuRequest::kDetach), 0,\n                                 kDfuIf, IsEmpty(), kUsbCtrlTimeout))\n      .WillOnce(Return(std::unexpected(kUsbErrorNoDevice)));\n\n  auto res \u003d device_-\u003eDfuDownload(std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e{1, 2});\n\n  ASSERT_FALSE(res);\n  EXPECT_EQ(res.error(), RtsError::kDeviceNotFound);\n}\n```\n4. **Add missing branch and boundary tests** for:\n   - `poll_timeout \u003d\u003d 0` fallback to `kDfuMinPollDelay` (`1ms`)\n   - `status \u003d\u003d kOk \u0026\u0026 state \u003d\u003d kDfuError` in `DfuPollIdle()`\n   - Pre-download recovery when the device starts in `kDfuDnloadBusy` and settles into `kDfuDnloadIdle` (verifying `DfuRequest::kAbort` is sent before block 0):\n```cpp\nTEST_F(RtsUsbDeviceDownloadTest, UsesMinPollDelayWhenPollTimeoutIsZero) {\n  fake_.busy_polls \u003d 1;\n  fake_.poll_timeout \u003d milliseconds(0);\n\n  ASSERT_TRUE(device_-\u003eDfuDownload(std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e{1, 2}));\n  EXPECT_EQ(slept_, (std::vector\u003cmilliseconds\u003e{kDfuMinPollDelay}));\n}\n\nTEST_F(RtsUsbDeviceDownloadTest, FailsWhenDeviceEntersErrorStateWithOkStatus) {\n  fake_.manifest_result \u003d DfuState::kDfuError;\n\n  auto res \u003d device_-\u003eDfuDownload(std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e{1, 2});\n\n  ASSERT_FALSE(res);\n  EXPECT_EQ(res.error(), RtsError::kDeviceRejected);\n}\n\nTEST_F(RtsUsbDeviceDownloadTest, AbortsAfterBusyRecoverySettlesInDnloadIdle) {\n  fake_.busy_polls \u003d 1;\n  fake_.state \u003d DfuState::kDfuDnloadIdle;\n\n  ASSERT_TRUE(device_-\u003eDfuDownload(std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e{1, 2}));\n  ASSERT_FALSE(fake_.requests.empty());\n  EXPECT_EQ(fake_.requests.front(), DfuRequest::kAbort);\n}\n```\n\nOther locations in this file:\n- **Lines 910–912** (`ShortWriteIsAnError`)\n- **Lines 929–945** (`ClearsStatusWhenDeviceIsInErrorState`)\n- **Lines 996–1005** (`DetachesAfterManifestSoDeviceBoots`)\n- **Lines 1007–1018** (`DetachFailureIsReported`)\n- **Lines 1055–1075** (`FailsWhenRecoveryStatusReadFails`, `ReportsShortStatusRead`)\n- **Lines 1090–1103** (`TimesOutWhenDeviceStaysBusy`)\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/b2c5d976-5204-4274-85f0-ebbdd5e79b54)",
